    <!-- SIMPLE FOOD GUIDE SECTION -->
    <div class="section-title">1. Food Made Simple (How to Eat)</div>
    <div class="note-box">
        <strong>The Kid-Friendly Rule:</strong> Think of your body like a sports car. 
        <strong>Protein</strong> builds the engine (muscle). 
        <strong>Carbs</strong> are the gasoline (energy for running/biking). 
        <strong>Fats</strong> keep the oil moving (healthy joints & hormones). 
        Since you want to lose fat from your belly/waist while keeping your muscle, we eat <u>high protein</u> and <u>medium energy</u>!
    </div>

    <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="card">
            <h3>🥩 What to Eat (Your Daily Menu)</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Protein (Builds Muscle):</strong> Chicken breast, ground turkey, egg whites, steak, salmon, Greek yogurt, protein powder. <i>Target: Eat a palm-sized portion of protein 4-5 times a day.</i></li>
                <li><strong>Carbs (Gives Energy):</strong> Oatmeal, white/brown rice, sweet potatoes, bananas, berries. <i>Eat these before and right after working out!</i></li>
                <li><strong>Healthy Fats (Joints & Hormones):</strong> Whole eggs, almonds, avocado, olive oil.</li>
                <li><strong>Veggies (Clean Gut):</strong> Asparagus, broccoli, spinach, cucumbers.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
            <h3>⏰ Simple Daily Eating Schedule</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Breakfast (Pre-Gym):</strong> 4 Egg whites + 2 whole eggs + 1/2 cup oatmeal + cinnamon.</li>
                <li><strong>Post-Gym Snack:</strong> 1.5 scoops protein powder + 1 banana.</li>
                <li><strong>Lunch:</strong> Palm of chicken or turkey + 1 cup rice + veggies.</li>
                <li><strong>Mid-Afternoon Snack:</strong> 1 cup Greek yogurt + 10-12 almonds.</li>
                <li><strong>Dinner:</strong> Steak or salmon + big green salad with olive oil.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CARDIO & MOBILITY SCHEDULE -->
    <div class="section-title">2. Cardio & Injury Safety Schedule</div>
    <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="card">
            <h3>🏃 Running & 🚴 Biking Rules</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Tuesday:</strong> Fast Sprint Interval Run (3 miles total, treadmill).</li>
                <li><strong>Wednesday:</strong> 5-Mile Steady Run (Sub-25 min target).</li>
                <li><strong>Saturday:</strong> Long Road Bike Ride (40 to 75 miles).</li>
                <li><i>Note: Do NOT run max speed on leg lifting days!</i></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
            <h3>🚑 Shoulder & Hamstring Protection</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Tight Hamstrings & Lower Back Pain:</strong> Do 30 "Elephant Walks" and 2 minutes of wall hamstring stretches before doing leg exercises!</li>
                <li><strong>Right Shoulder Pain:</strong> Always do 2 sets of light Cable Face Pulls before bench pressing. Never lower dumbbells past your chest.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

